Fix a botched find-replace in the installed CMake config package.

v1.0.1 ships `find_dependency(pybifind_dependencyCONFIG REQUIRED)` — the string
"nd11 " was replaced with "find_dependency", turning "pybind11 CONFIG" into
"pybifind_dependencyCONFIG". Any consumer calling find_package(falcon-qarray-device)
fails with "Could not find a package configuration file provided by
pybifind_dependencyCONFIG".

Remove this patch once the fix is released upstream.

diff --git a/cmake/falcon-qarray-device-config.cmake.in b/cmake/falcon-qarray-device-config.cmake.in
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/cmake/falcon-qarray-device-config.cmake.in
+++ b/cmake/falcon-qarray-device-config.cmake.in
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 include(CMakeFindDependencyMacro)
 
 find_dependency(Python3 COMPONENTS Interpreter Development REQUIRED)
-find_dependency(pybifind_dependencyCONFIG REQUIRED)
+find_dependency(pybind11 CONFIG REQUIRED)
 
 include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/falcon-qarray-device-targets.cmake")
 
